   cannot ban ordinal arithmetic without failing itself.
b. SOP line 1757 words GD-05 as "no `sealed` string outside those two allowlisted files".
   Implemented as a use rule, not a bare-token rule: the token appears today in
   src/absump/paths.py, src/absump/db.py, ops/*.sh and dbt/profiles.yml.example as a
   directory name and in prose, so a bare-token rule would be red at rest on files this
   step does not own. What is enforced is that the label may not reach the routing column,
   a view name or a fact-table read, by any spelling.
